What this licence does not cover

- The generated film (`outputs/film_9x16.mp4`, `outputs/film_16x9.mp4`), the
  generated panels, keyframes and portraits in `outputs/`, and the narration
  audio. Their terms come from the models that produced them: Gemini TTS
  (Google) and MiniMax image-01 (MiniMax), whose generative-output terms are
  the owner's to confirm — see `ETHICS.md`.
- The story. "Eat, My Clothes, Eat!" is a traditional Ethiopian folk tale,
  retold here; the retelling in `storyboard.json`, `STORY.md` and the film is
  the author's.
- The bundled fonts in `comic/media/` and `editor/fonts/`: DM Sans, Bangers
  and Noto Sans Ethiopic, each under the SIL Open Font Licence 1.1, which
  applies to those files instead.
- The Rust dependency `fframes` (MIT) and FFmpeg/x264 (LGPL/GPL), which are
  linked tools, not part of this repository's code.
